From: FlaxAdvisors
Subject: add NetFn 0x32 host-interface inventory bootstrap handler

TP26 BIOS populates BMC inventory via AMI's Redfish Host Interface: a small
KCS NetFn 0x32 bootstrap (device-list probe 0x2a, device-status 0x3d, credential
issue 0x5d, acks 0xaa/0xab) then an authenticated inventory push over the USB
vNIC.  This adds the native bootstrap handler so POST proceeds and the BIOS is
issued the host-interface credential.  Response bytes transliterate the
offline-tested tools/netfn32/netfn32_model.py (ground-truthed from a live OEM
KCS capture).

